{%- comment -%}
  Capture-phase click interceptor for the LP product form's Add To Cart
  button.

  Why this hooks click and not submit: the ATC button has no
  type="submit" and no form-submit handler — its only listener is an
  Alpine @click that opens the off-canvas cart. The actual POST to
  /cart/add.js is performed by Rebuy's SmartCartV2, which binds its own
  click handler on the ATC button, reads the form (via serializeArray),
  and fetches /cart/add.js directly. The form's `submit` event is never
  dispatched, so a submit listener never fires.

  Why this matters: Recharge's storefront app embed renders a hidden
  `<select name="selling_plan">` (the plan dropdown) inside the product
  form whose default selected option carries the subscription plan id.
  Native FormData and jQuery's serializeArray pick it up regardless of
  what our Alpine UI shows. Recharge also injects radios named
  `selling_plan_<plan_id>` with values "subsave" / "onetime"; the
  "subsave" radio is checked at page load and our UI doesn't sync with
  it either. Either source on its own is enough for Shopify's cart to
  add the item as a subscription, since `selling_plan_<id>=<any>` is
  treated as equivalent to `selling_plan=<id>`.

  The fix: a capture-phase click listener on the ATC button. Capture
  phase fires before any bubble-phase listener Rebuy or anything else
  binds, so we can disable the offending inputs synchronously before
  Rebuy reads the form. Disabled inputs are skipped by both
  serializeArray and FormData.

  We never re-enable inputs once disabled. Our own
  `<input name="selling_plan">` is re-created by `<template x-if>` in
  product-form__subscription-options-lp.liquid whenever sellingPlanType
  flips back to "subscription", so subscription-mode ATC continues to
  serialize the correct plan id from our Alpine input.

  Required parameter: section_id — the id of the section's root
  element, used to scope the selector to this section's form (avoids
  :not() descendant matching, which is flaky across browsers).
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    var sectionEl = document.getElementById({{ section_id | json }});
    if (!sectionEl) return;

    var form = sectionEl.querySelector('form.product-top__form');
    if (!form) return;

    var atcButton = form.querySelector('button.add-to-cart');
    if (!atcButton) return;

    atcButton.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var sellingPlanType = null;

      if (window.Alpine && typeof Alpine.$data === 'function') {
        try {
          var state = Alpine.$data(form);
          if (state) sellingPlanType = state.sellingPlanType;
        } catch (_) {
          // Alpine present but data unavailable — fall through to radio.
        }
      }

      if (sellingPlanType == null) {
        var checked = form.querySelector('input[name="purchase_selector"]:checked');
        sellingPlanType = checked ? checked.value : null;
      }

      if (sellingPlanType !== 'one-time') return;

      // No tag-name prefix on these selectors — Recharge contributes a
      // `<select name="selling_plan">` (the plan dropdown) as well as
      // `<input type="radio" name="selling_plan_<id>">` controls, and
      // both need to be neutralized. disabled controls of any tag type
      // are skipped by both FormData and serializeArray.
      var controls = form.querySelectorAll(
        '[name="selling_plan"], [name^="selling_plan_"]'
      );
      for (var i = 0; i < controls.length; i++) {
        controls[i].disabled = true;
      }
    }, true);
  })();
</script>
